A repoducible example is using the the actionButton widget <http://shiny.rstudio.com/gallery/widgets-gallery.html> with a duplicate button (below). I may be missing something obvious.. help much appreciated.

thank you!

# ui.r
shinyUI(fluidPage(

  # Copy the line below to make an action button
  actionButton("action", label = "Action"), #only this one increments input$action
  actionButton("action", label = "Action"), #this one does not

  hr(),
  fluidRow(column(2, verbatimTextOutput("value")))

))

# server.r
shinyServer(function(input, output) {

  # You can access the value of the widget with input$action, e.g.
  output$value <- renderPrint({ input$action })

})

